    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14985" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dūrĭus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dūrēus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δούριος</span> or
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δούρειος</span>, equus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the Trojan horse</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Aur.
				Vict. Orig. 1</span></i>; Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest.
				p. 82, 12</span></i>. —<b>Poet.</b>
			transf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">duria nox,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the night in which the Greeks descended from
						the interior of the horse</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 2, 573</span></i>
			; cf. durateus.</div>
